# =============================================================================
# passes_and_oauth — Apple Wallet signing material
# =============================================================================
# The rule is the same one the root .gitignore states: a secret committed once
# is public for ever, because it stays in the history and in every clone.
#
# What is safe here is narrow. A .cer is the PUBLIC half of a certificate and
# cannot sign anything on its own. Everything that can — the private key, the
# .p12 that pairs it with the certificate, the OAuth client secret — is denied
# below, by extension rather than by filename, so that dropping a new file in
# this directory does not quietly make it committable.
# =============================================================================

# Deny everything, then allow back the five public certificates by name.
# Written this way round on purpose: a new secret dropped in here is ignored by
# default, where an allow-list of denials would have to be remembered.
*

!.gitignore
!README.md

!giftcard_pass.cer
!loyalty_pass.cer
!membership_pass.cer
!promotion_pass.cer
!staffcard_pass.cer

# The fallback pass artwork, which is ordinary public brand imagery and has to
# travel with the code: wallet_apple.js reads it at build time for every pass a
# venue has not put its own logo on, so a deployment without it signs passes
# that will not install. The directory needs unignoring before the files in it
# can be — `*` above matches the directory, and git never looks inside an
# excluded directory to find an exception.
!assets/
!assets/*.png

# Belt and braces. If one of the names above is ever reused for something that
# is not a certificate, these still hold — and they document the intent.
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
*.certSigningRequest
client_secret*
*secret*
*.json
